# M3 restart probe — what survives a `kill -9` of the process that started a render.
#
# HOW TO REPRODUCE (a stranger, from a clean clone):
#
#   node deepblend/tools/create-demo-project.mjs        # if .deepblend/ has no project yet
#   node deepblend/tools/m3-restart-probe.mjs restart   # ~15 min at 1920x1080; --frames 4 --kill-at 2 for ~2
#
# RE-MEASURED 2026-09-14 (round 32), against revision r0002 — the store's CURRENT revision. This probe
# used to default to the literal 'r0029' and died with `ENOENT … /revisions/r0029/scene-spec.json` once
# the demo project moved on, which is why the target is now derived from `project.json` and why the
# revision it used is recorded here (re-run with DEEPBLEND_PROBE_REVISION=rXXXX to reproduce an older
# reading).
#
# WHAT IT IS EVIDENCE FOR (`recovery.md` §1): the Blender child OUTLIVES the Host that started it, the
# fsynced journal survives, the ledger rebuilt from the frame files is right, and resuming renders
# exactly the missing set without touching a frame that was already there. Unchanged from the M3 run;
# the frame count differs only because the demo project's current revision is shorter.

